Adapted parts. They were rewritten for the Ontology Studio model (Apache Ossie) and Unity Catalog
catalog.schema.table names; some rule and message texts follow the originals closely.
- modules/sqlcheck.py: the read-only guard, column lineage, join, fan-out, text-value, numeric-scale,
  grouping, integer-division and placeholder checks, and value lookups (from auto-ontology-mcp
  sqlcheck.py, validation.py and structure.py, which follow Auto Ontology's db_probe and
  sql_parse_validation).
- modules/answering.py: lexical search scoring, join paths, the entity coverage check and its
  extraction rules, readiness (from auto-ontology-mcp search.py, naming.py, graph.py, guidance.py and
  service.py, which follow Auto Ontology's entity coverage and text-to-SQL prompts).
- modules/ask.py: SQL-writing rules in the answer prompt (from auto-ontology-mcp guidance.py).
- modules/modeling.py: re-scan drift and table filters, the modeling worklist, unlinked identifier columns,
  observed joins, default joins for multi-role relationships, filter suggestions from small value sets,
  testing expressions before saving, the change log and the model checks (from auto-ontology-mcp
  service.py scan_datasource, get_modeling_worklist, list_relationships, suggest_sql_attributes,
  save_sql_attribute, recent_changes and its review_ontology prompt).
- modules/llm_enrich.py: the grain, column-description and variant-table rules in the enrichment prompt (from
  auto-ontology-mcp guidance.py TERM_RULES, which follow Auto Ontology's term extractor).

Adapted directly from NVIDIA Auto Ontology (auto_ontology/, Apache-2.0):
- modules/profiling.py: the personal-data rules (pii_detection/rules.py; their patterns are kept as they are,
  table-name prefixes such as dim_ and silver_ were added), the date-format inference (semantic/date_format.py;
  YYYY-MM was added), the sample rules (semantic/visit_enter.py: the 5 most common values, text of 30 characters or
  less) and the sampling circuit breaker with its connectivity markers (visit_enter.py, connectors/db_errors.py; markers of the
  Databricks SQL connector were added).
- modules/discovery.py: the same-key (vertical split) join and the value-search ambiguity guard
  (semantic/concepts.py, semantic/fk_values.py), without the LLM confirmation step.
- modules/llm_enrich.py: a description that only repeats the name counts as missing (semantic/deterministic.py).
- modules/ask.py: the default-join, NULL and date-format rules in the answer prompt (react/prompts.py,
  semantic/date_format.py).

